    {
      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "TWICE — Likey",
      "content": "Standard negation. \"It doesn't change.\"\n\nLikey is TWICE's 2017 title track, and it's about the very specific, very modern anxiety of curating yourself for social media while waiting for one particular person's reaction. She's not posting for the world — she's posting for a like from someone whose opinion actually matters, and admitting that a heart-shaped button can't really carry what she's trying to say.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-지 않다**, which means \"not, negation.\" We'll see how TWICE uses it in \"Likey.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **변하다** — to change\n- **끝** — end\n- **변하지 않다** — to not change\n- **끝나지 않다** — to not end\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
